A||N||4||007DOUG||4 cyl. Holley TBI w/o other upgrades? Worth it?||||5||
Z||000000||007DOUG||09-06-2000||10:41 PM||||On the 84-86 4cyl, If I add the aftermarket Holley TBI without upgrading the intake and head, Will I notice any difference in performance?<P>Anyone here add only the Holley TBI? How does it feel? <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||09-06-2000||11:31 PM||||Probably not. I was going to try to built my 4cyl, but everyone said it's not worth it. When I thought about it, it's true. I would have just wasted my time and money, for a barely noticeable difference.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kslish||09-07-2000||12:04 PM||||I'm planning on doing the same thing (although I may also do the Hooker exhaust header).  I'm shooting to get about 110-120hp out of my Duke to make me a little more happy during my everyday commute (I've got a GT also but the 4-cyl wins out for my daily driver since it basically only sips fuel).  I'm not looking for tire spinning performance or anything.  Anyways, to take advantage of the bigger bore of the Holley TBI you should bore out the opening of the intake manifold some.  The Holley has a 2-inch bore and stock is only 1.6 inches.  As a result the opening in the stock intake manifold is only 1.6 inches.  Mounting the Holly TBI onto an unmodified manifold would probably provide only a minor improvement at best since the small opening in the manifold would act like a restrictor plate (and for those that follow NASCAR, you know what restrictor plates do to horsepower).  So basically, enlarging the 1.6 inch opening in the manifold will permit the engine to take advantage of the increased air capacity of the Holley TBI.  The discontinued Holley intake manifold had a 2-inch opening to match their TBI....wish I had one of those.  I'm not sure if you can bore the stock manifold opening out to 2 inches or not (haven't pulled off my stock TBI yet) but Darrell Morse (I think that is his name) bores stock manifolds out to 1.85 inches for a small charge if you don't want to attempt it yourself.  I'll see if I can find his e-mail address in my notes.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fotofrank||09-07-2000||01:42 PM||||  I have a Holley TBI. I bored the input out but not enough. I still sence an improvement. I recomend the TBI opening to be bored to 2 pluse inchs and the stock deflector reformed and installed. without this pice you may feel a hesitation when accelerating. While the intake is off port match the intake to the head. check my site.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||10
